{
  "about": "Stage 14 (decisions S14-94 to S14-99; Book 7 sections 13 and 14, Book 9 section 03): how every island scene changes with the season, for the renderer only. `ramps` recolours the ground, decal and plant sheets (the sheets `sheets` names; a name ending in `_` is a prefix) palette step to palette step along Book 7's ramps, never to an ad-hoc colour; spring is the look as drawn (the approved art, the game's first days). `bloom` is the heather in flower, late summer into early autumn. `zones` gives each scene snow on its high ground in winter (0 to 1), whether its still pools freeze, the seasons its upper stream shrinks to its pools (S14-5), mist, and the seasons anemones open in its pools; `default` covers a scene not listed, so a new scene changes with the seasons from the start. `life` keeps a share of each kind of wildlife by season (birds come and go), and `zoneLife` overrides it for a scene. `falls` puts Book 9's waterfalls on the zone's stream (a block of the island grid, snapped to the stream at the lip), and `mouths` names the edge a stream leaves by where it meets no sea. `seasonless` lists the scenes the book keeps unchanged by season, with the reason. `zones.<zone>.ramps` adds a scene's own steps for a season (the deep passage's spring slime, decision S14-143), and `seeps` the seasons its walls run with meltwater. `interiors` gives the two interiors their own light in place of the outdoor grade (decision S14-144): no cloud shadows, shafts or sun shadows, the phase whose ambient they start from, a grade, a damp haze, the light off their water drifting in patches, and pools of light from their openings (tiles; with a fact, only while it holds). `sheets` names every sheet the seasons recolour (decision S14-146); a scene in `seasonless` is never recoloured.",
